    "brightness": { "liquid": 1.06 },
    "reduced": 0.94,
    "control": {
      "_": "The controls on liquid glass (4.1): pressed, a glass lights up (white over it at \"pressLight\") and grows by \"pressScale\", on the \"bouncy\" spring; the prominent glass (the main button, the chosen chip) is the accent (or the ink) at \"prominent\"; a field is a hollow of thin glass, its shade at the kind's \"hollow\" inside its top edge. Laid in a light surface (a sheet, a card, thick glass), white on white loses its edges (4.1.1): what floats keeps its light on top and takes the ink at its bottom edge and a contact shadow; a field's hollow takes the ink under its top edge and the light at its bottom; a form's card takes the ink at its bottom edge only (the values: each platform's \"nested\" constants).",
